FullPath returns a matched route full path. For not found routes
returns an empty string.

	router.GET("/user/:id", func(c *gin.Context) {
	    c.FullPath() == "/user/:id" // true
	})

func  FullPath() string

Get returns the value for the given key, ie: (value, true).
If the value does not exist it returns (nil, false)

func  Get(key any) (value any, exists bool)

GetPostFormArray returns a slice of strings for a given form key, plus
a boolean value whether at least one value exists for the given key.

func  GetPostFormArray(key string) (values []string, ok bool)

GetPostFormMap returns a map for a given form key, plus a boolean value
whether at least one value exists for the given key.

func  GetPostFormMap(key string) (map[string]string, bool)

GetQueryArray returns a slice of strings for a given query key, plus
a boolean value whether at least one value exists for the given key.

func  GetQueryArray(key string) (values []string, ok bool)

GetQueryMap returns a map for a given query key, plus a boolean value
whether at least one value exists for the given key.

func  GetQueryMap(key string) (map[string]string, bool)

JSON serializes the given struct as JSON into the response body.
It also sets the Content-Type as "application/json".

func  JSON(code int, obj any)

PDF writes the given PDF binary data into the response body.
It also sets the Content-Type as "application/pdf".

func  PDF(code int, data []byte)

Param returns the value of the URL param.
It is a shortcut for c.Params.ByName(key)

	router.GET("/user/:id", func(c *gin.Context) {
	    // a GET request to /user/john
	    id := c.Param("id") // id == "john"
	    // a GET request to /user/john/
	    id := c.Param("id") // id == "/john/"
	})

func  Param(key string) string

PostForm returns the specified key from a POST urlencoded form or multipart form
when it exists, otherwise it returns an empty string `("")`.

func  PostForm(key string) (value string)

PostFormArray returns a slice of strings for a given form key.
The length of the slice depends on the number of params with the given key.

func  PostFormArray(key string) (values []string)

PureJSON serializes the given struct as JSON into the response body.
PureJSON, unlike JSON, does not replace special html characters with their unicode entities.

func  PureJSON(code int, obj any)

QueryArray returns a slice of strings for a given query key.
The length of the slice depends on the number of params with the given key.

func  QueryArray(key string) (values []string)

Set is used to store a new key/value pair exclusively for this context.
It also lazy initializes c.Keys if it was not used previously.

func  Set(key any, value any)

ShouldBindJSON is a shortcut for c.ShouldBindWith(obj, binding.JSON).

Example:

	POST /user
	Content-Type: application/json

	Request Body:
	{
		"name": "Manu",
		"age": 20
	}

	type User struct {
		Name string `json:"name"`
		Age  int    `json:"age"`
	}

	var user User
	if err := c.ShouldBindJSON(&user); err != nil {
		c.JSON(http.StatusBadRequest, gin.H{"error": err.Error()})
		return
	}
	c.JSON(http.StatusOK, user)

func  ShouldBindJSON(obj any) error

